1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,279
Your API is slow. Or it is broken. Or the mistake is in your own request.

2
00:00:05,829 --> 00:00:07,253
How do you find out which?

3
00:00:07,253 --> 00:00:08,185
You do not guess.

4
00:00:08,185 --> 00:00:10,102
You look at the whole conversation,

5
00:00:10,102 --> 00:00:10,650
with curl.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:15,018
Today you learn five moves: see everything with verbose mode,

7
00:00:15,018 --> 00:00:16,395
read and send headers,

8
00:00:16,395 --> 00:00:17,459
measure the time,

9
00:00:17,459 --> 00:00:18,586
use the exit code,

10
00:00:18,586 --> 00:00:21,653
and tag a request so you can find it in the logs.

11
00:00:22,203 --> 00:00:27,131
These five moves cover most of what a dev ops engineer does to test an endpoint.

12
00:00:29,181 --> 00:00:32,296
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

13
00:00:32,846 --> 00:00:35,896
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

14
00:00:36,446 --> 00:00:37,799
Ask for product one,

15
00:00:37,799 --> 00:00:39,963
and show the whole conversation.

16
00:00:39,963 --> 00:00:40,707
Type: curl,

17
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:41,316
dash s V,

18
00:00:41,316 --> 00:00:42,127
the address,

19
00:00:42,127 --> 00:00:42,398
two,

20
00:00:42,398 --> 00:00:43,277
greater than,

21
00:00:43,277 --> 00:00:44,224
ampersand one,

22
00:00:44,224 --> 00:00:44,562
pipe,

23
00:00:44,562 --> 00:00:44,900
grep,

24
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:45,306
quote,

25
00:00:45,306 --> 00:00:45,712
caret,

26
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,253
bracket,

27
00:00:46,253 --> 00:00:46,929
less than,

28
00:00:46,929 --> 00:00:47,808
greater than,

29
00:00:47,808 --> 00:00:48,755
close bracket,

30
00:00:48,755 --> 00:00:49,161
space,

31
00:00:49,161 --> 00:00:49,702
bracket,

32
00:00:49,702 --> 00:00:50,378
capital A,

33
00:00:50,378 --> 00:00:51,392
dash capital Z,

34
00:00:51,392 --> 00:00:52,339
close bracket,

35
00:00:52,339 --> 00:00:52,745
quote.

36
00:00:53,295 --> 00:00:57,360
Every line that starts with a greater than sign is what curl sent.

37
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:58,038
The method,

38
00:00:58,038 --> 00:00:58,592
the path,

39
00:00:58,592 --> 00:00:59,147
the host,

40
00:00:59,147 --> 00:01:00,502
and the accept header.

41
00:01:00,502 --> 00:01:02,042
Curl added those for you.

42
00:01:02,592 --> 00:01:06,204
Every line that starts with a less than sign is what came back.

43
00:01:06,204 --> 00:01:07,121
The status line,

44
00:01:07,121 --> 00:01:08,096
then the headers.

45
00:01:08,646 --> 00:01:11,267
Two of them are custom: X API version,

46
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:12,509
and X request I D.

47
00:01:12,509 --> 00:01:13,475
Remember them.

48
00:01:13,475 --> 00:01:15,131
You will use both today.

49
00:01:15,681 --> 00:01:18,527
Verbose mode is the first tool to reach for.

50
00:01:18,527 --> 00:01:20,596
It shows the whole conversation,

51
00:01:20,596 --> 00:01:21,825
in both directions.

52
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:27,800
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

53
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:31,401
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

54
00:01:31,951 --> 00:01:33,697
Ask for only the headers,

55
00:01:33,697 --> 00:01:34,605
with no body.

56
00:01:34,605 --> 00:01:35,373
Type: curl,

57
00:01:35,373 --> 00:01:36,560
dash s capital I,

58
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,586
then the address of products.

59
00:01:39,136 --> 00:01:41,453
Content type says what the body is.

60
00:01:41,453 --> 00:01:44,963
X API version says which version of the API answered.

61
00:01:44,963 --> 00:01:47,413
Headers are labels about the message.

62
00:01:47,963 --> 00:01:49,781
You can send headers too.

63
00:01:49,781 --> 00:01:51,526
Dash capital H adds one.

64
00:01:51,526 --> 00:01:54,798
The accept header says which format you want.

65
00:01:54,798 --> 00:01:55,598
Type: curl,

66
00:01:55,598 --> 00:01:56,107
dash s,

67
00:01:56,107 --> 00:01:57,198
dash capital H,

68
00:01:57,198 --> 00:01:57,634
quote,

69
00:01:57,634 --> 00:01:58,143
accept,

70
00:01:58,143 --> 00:01:58,580
colon,

71
00:01:58,580 --> 00:01:59,816
text slash C S V,

72
00:01:59,816 --> 00:02:00,252
quote,

73
00:02:00,252 --> 00:02:01,488
then the address.

74
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:02,852
Same address,

75
00:02:02,852 --> 00:02:03,917
different format.

76
00:02:03,917 --> 00:02:06,108
The server read your accept header,

77
00:02:06,108 --> 00:02:08,801
and answered with C S V instead of jay son.

78
00:02:09,351 --> 00:02:14,620
That is content negotiation. You ask with headers, and the server decides what to send.

79
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:20,595
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

80
00:02:21,145 --> 00:02:24,196
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

81
00:02:24,746 --> 00:02:26,253
Is an endpoint slow?

82
00:02:26,253 --> 00:02:27,082
Measure it.

83
00:02:27,082 --> 00:02:27,911
Type: curl,

84
00:02:27,911 --> 00:02:28,439
dash s,

85
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:28,966
dash O,

86
00:02:28,966 --> 00:02:30,549
slash dev slash null,

87
00:02:30,549 --> 00:02:31,076
dash W,

88
00:02:31,076 --> 00:02:31,528
quote,

89
00:02:31,528 --> 00:02:32,131
percent,

90
00:02:32,131 --> 00:02:32,583
brace,

91
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:33,563
H T T P code,

92
00:02:33,563 --> 00:02:34,015
brace,

93
00:02:34,015 --> 00:02:34,467
space,

94
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:35,070
percent,

95
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:35,522
brace,

96
00:02:35,522 --> 00:02:36,351
time total,

97
00:02:36,351 --> 00:02:36,803
brace,

98
00:02:36,803 --> 00:02:37,708
backslash N,

99
00:02:37,708 --> 00:02:38,160
quote,

100
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,441
then the address,

101
00:02:39,441 --> 00:02:40,194
slash API,

102
00:02:40,194 --> 00:02:41,023
slash fast.

103
00:02:41,573 --> 00:02:44,385
Dash O to dev null throws the body away.

104
00:02:44,385 --> 00:02:48,040
Dash W prints only what we ask for: the status code,

105
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:50,149
and the total time in seconds.

106
00:02:50,699 --> 00:02:56,182
Now the report endpoint. Same command, new path. Type it again, with report at the end.

107
00:02:58,332 --> 00:03:00,162
Under a hundredth of a second,

108
00:03:00,162 --> 00:03:01,992
against almost a whole second.

109
00:03:01,992 --> 00:03:04,188
Now you know which endpoint is slow,

110
00:03:04,188 --> 00:03:05,042
with a number,

111
00:03:05,042 --> 00:03:06,140
and not a feeling.

112
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:09,245
Time total counts everything: connecting,

113
00:03:09,245 --> 00:03:09,744
waiting,

114
00:03:09,744 --> 00:03:10,741
and downloading.

115
00:03:10,741 --> 00:03:12,237
That is enough to start.

116
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:18,212
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

117
00:03:18,762 --> 00:03:21,813
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

118
00:03:22,363 --> 00:03:24,355
Ask for product ninety-nine,

119
00:03:24,355 --> 00:03:26,348
then print curl's exit code.

120
00:03:26,348 --> 00:03:27,131
Type: curl,

121
00:03:27,131 --> 00:03:27,629
dash s,

122
00:03:27,629 --> 00:03:28,483
the address,

123
00:03:28,483 --> 00:03:29,194
semicolon,

124
00:03:29,194 --> 00:03:29,550
echo,

125
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:29,977
quote,

126
00:03:29,977 --> 00:03:30,831
exit equals,

127
00:03:30,831 --> 00:03:31,329
dollar,

128
00:03:31,329 --> 00:03:32,325
question mark,

129
00:03:32,325 --> 00:03:32,752
quote.

130
00:03:33,302 --> 00:03:34,951
The body says not found.

131
00:03:34,951 --> 00:03:36,325
But look: exit zero.

132
00:03:36,325 --> 00:03:37,631
Curl itself worked.

133
00:03:37,631 --> 00:03:40,310
A four oh four is still a valid answer,

134
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:42,028
so curl calls it success.

135
00:03:42,578 --> 00:03:46,183
Add dash F, for fail. Type the same command, with S F.

136
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:49,613
Now curl prints nothing,

137
00:03:49,613 --> 00:03:51,216
and exits with twenty-two.

138
00:03:51,216 --> 00:03:54,853
Twenty-two means: the server answered with an error status.

139
00:03:55,403 --> 00:03:57,584
This is how a smoke test works.

140
00:03:57,584 --> 00:03:58,851
One curl dash S F,

141
00:03:58,851 --> 00:04:01,595
and the exit code is your pass or fail.

142
00:04:01,595 --> 00:04:04,128
Scripts and CI pipelines stop on it.

143
00:04:06,178 --> 00:04:10,103
Same shop, new session. Go in. Type: CD, cloud cart.

144
00:04:10,653 --> 00:04:13,704
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

145
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:17,330
Tag a request with an I D that you choose.

146
00:04:17,330 --> 00:04:18,136
Type: curl,

147
00:04:18,136 --> 00:04:18,648
dash s,

148
00:04:18,648 --> 00:04:19,747
dash capital H,

149
00:04:19,747 --> 00:04:20,186
quote,

150
00:04:20,186 --> 00:04:21,212
X request I D,

151
00:04:21,212 --> 00:04:21,651
colon,

152
00:04:21,651 --> 00:04:23,116
demo dash forty-two,

153
00:04:23,116 --> 00:04:23,556
quote,

154
00:04:23,556 --> 00:04:24,068
dash O,

155
00:04:24,068 --> 00:04:25,606
slash dev slash null,

156
00:04:25,606 --> 00:04:27,950
then the address of product one.

157
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,389
The API writes that I D into its log.

158
00:04:31,389 --> 00:04:33,419
Look at the last log line.

159
00:04:33,419 --> 00:04:34,278
Type: tail,

160
00:04:34,278 --> 00:04:34,824
dash N,

161
00:04:34,824 --> 00:04:35,136
one,

162
00:04:35,136 --> 00:04:36,073
API dot log.

163
00:04:36,623 --> 00:04:38,221
There it is: the method,

164
00:04:38,221 --> 00:04:38,820
the path,

165
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:39,552
the status,

166
00:04:39,552 --> 00:04:40,151
the time,

167
00:04:40,151 --> 00:04:41,016
and your I D.

168
00:04:41,016 --> 00:04:43,279
When a customer reports a problem,

169
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:46,607
an I D like this finds the exact line in the logs.

170
00:04:47,157 --> 00:04:47,539
Last,

171
00:04:47,539 --> 00:04:53,721
a tiny API client: a script that asks four endpoints and prints each status code.

172
00:04:53,721 --> 00:04:56,011
Type: dot slash codes dot S H.

173
00:04:56,561 --> 00:04:57,346
Two hundred,

174
00:04:57,346 --> 00:04:58,132
two hundred,

175
00:04:58,132 --> 00:04:58,984
four oh four,

176
00:04:58,984 --> 00:04:59,769
two hundred.

177
00:04:59,769 --> 00:05:04,091
A script like this is a smoke test you can run after every deploy.

178
00:05:04,641 --> 00:05:08,204
Stop the shop. Type: dot slash stop dot S H.

179
00:05:10,254 --> 00:05:12,707
Curl is not the only tool for this job.

180
00:05:13,257 --> 00:05:15,289
Your browser has developer tools.

181
00:05:15,289 --> 00:05:18,306
The network tab shows every request a page makes,

182
00:05:18,306 --> 00:05:20,276
with its headers and its timing.

183
00:05:20,826 --> 00:05:21,941
Graphical clients,

184
00:05:21,941 --> 00:05:23,489
such as Postman or Bruno,

185
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:24,666
save your requests,

186
00:05:24,666 --> 00:05:26,586
so a whole team can share them.

187
00:05:27,136 --> 00:05:31,104
Command line clients, like http ie, print prettier output.

188
00:05:31,654 --> 00:05:37,329
And scripts: a few lines of curl, run after every deploy, turn testing into automation.

189
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,042
Pick any of them.

190
00:05:39,042 --> 00:05:41,644
The ideas are always the same: method,

191
00:05:41,644 --> 00:05:41,986
path,

192
00:05:41,986 --> 00:05:42,534
headers,

193
00:05:42,534 --> 00:05:42,876
body,

194
00:05:42,876 --> 00:05:43,355
status,

195
00:05:43,355 --> 00:05:44,108
and timing.

196
00:05:46,158 --> 00:05:48,931
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

197
00:05:49,481 --> 00:05:51,983
The lab is lab sixty-nine dot S H,

198
00:05:51,983 --> 00:05:55,735
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

199
00:05:55,735 --> 00:05:57,206
slash it dash waves,

200
00:05:57,206 --> 00:05:58,898
slash dev ops dash A I.

201
00:05:58,898 --> 00:06:00,590
Install it like before,

202
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:01,768
then run lab up,

203
00:06:01,768 --> 00:06:05,225
and work inside slash opt slash lab sixty-nine.

204
00:06:05,775 --> 00:06:08,971
One: read the API version from a response header,

205
00:06:08,971 --> 00:06:11,123
and write it in answers dot text,

206
00:06:11,123 --> 00:06:12,362
like this: version,

207
00:06:12,362 --> 00:06:12,753
colon,

208
00:06:12,753 --> 00:06:13,797
then the number.

209
00:06:14,347 --> 00:06:17,126
Two: ask for the product list as C S V,

210
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:18,836
using the accept header,

211
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:21,259
and save it in products dot C S V.

212
00:06:21,809 --> 00:06:24,220
Three: time slash API slash fast,

213
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:26,193
and slash API slash report.

214
00:06:26,193 --> 00:06:29,189
Write the slower one in answers dot text,

215
00:06:29,189 --> 00:06:30,650
after the word slow,

216
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:31,089
colon.

217
00:06:31,639 --> 00:06:33,441
Four: write smoke dot S H.

218
00:06:33,441 --> 00:06:35,452
It takes an optional address,

219
00:06:35,452 --> 00:06:37,255
and exits zero on success,

220
00:06:37,255 --> 00:06:39,057
and non zero on any error.

221
00:06:39,057 --> 00:06:41,068
Even when the server is down.

222
00:06:41,618 --> 00:06:45,565
Five: send any request with the header X request I D,

223
00:06:45,565 --> 00:06:46,012
colon,

224
00:06:46,012 --> 00:06:47,949
lab sixty-nine dash trace,

225
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:50,109
so it appears in the API log.

226
00:06:50,659 --> 00:06:53,197
Then run lab check. Five pass lines.

227
00:06:55,247 --> 00:06:57,231
Six points, and you need all six.

228
00:06:57,781 --> 00:06:59,658
The checker shows five pass lines.

229
00:07:00,208 --> 00:07:03,984
You can read the request and the response in curl verbose output.

230
00:07:04,534 --> 00:07:06,433
You can send a header, and read one.

231
00:07:06,983 --> 00:07:10,226
You can measure an endpoint, and name the slow one with a number.

232
00:07:10,776 --> 00:07:15,981
You can explain why curl exits zero on a four oh four, and how dash F changes that.

233
00:07:16,531 --> 00:07:19,262
You ran lab down, and nothing is left listening.

234
00:07:19,812 --> 00:07:21,433
To pass, you need all six.

235
00:07:23,483 --> 00:07:26,320
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

236
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:29,089
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

